{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Build Sector Revenue Pivot & Combo Chart Results Season",
  "scenario": "It's late March, results season is live, and your research desk needs a quick sector-wise revenue summary split by quarters. You have raw quarterly data for ten major Indian companies across Banking, IT, Pharma, and Auto sectors. Build a PivotTable to answer the senior's rapid-fire questions — then create a results-season combo chart showing Infosys quarterly revenue trend with margin overlay.",
  "instructions": "Build a PivotTable from the Data sheet, reshape it to answer five escalating questions, and use GETPIVOTDATA formulas to pull specific figures into the Answers sheet; create one combo chart on the Chart sheet.",
  "learning_objective": "Build a PivotTable from tidy data, reshape it by dragging fields into Rows/Columns/Values zones, apply % of Grand Total formatting, group dates by quarter, and use GETPIVOTDATA to fetch pivot values robustly across reshuffles.",
  "hints": [
    "A PivotTable never touches your source data — it builds a private cached copy. After editing the raw Data sheet, always Refresh (Alt+F5) before trusting any pivot number.",
    "GETPIVOTDATA syntax: first argument is the Values field name (e.g. 'Revenue'), second is any cell inside the pivot (e.g. $A$3), then field–item pairs for each dimension (e.g. 'Sector', 'Pharma', 'Year', 2026).",
    "When dragging fields into Values zone, numeric columns default to Sum (correct for revenue), but if you see Count instead, the column has hidden blanks or text—go back to Data sheet and clean it (Session 3.7). For the chart, Infosys margin is already cleaned as a decimal (0.185 = 18.5%), so it will sum correctly in the pivot."
  ],
